{"caveats":[{"caveat_id":"caveat_90b171099906a6d8","evidence_ids":["ev_03c79b1bae942092"],"text":"The potentials were measured relative to the Ag/AgCl reference electrode and converted to the RHE scale in 1 M KOH (pH = 14) using the following equation: Evs RHE=Evs Ag/AgCl+"}],"characterization":[{"entity_id":"char_c586a5b655618005","evidence_ids":["ev_e6e06180466f9d49"],"output":null,"settings":{},"technique":"gas chromatography"}],"evidence":[{"char_end":600,"char_start":437,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":69837,"document_char_start":69674,"evidence_id":"ev_fe33583ca0f97f77","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst ink was prepared by sonicating a mixture of 3 mg catalyst, 500 μL deionized water, 460 μLabsoluteethanol,and40μLof5wt%Nafion for 1.5 h in an ice bath.","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8dc5b55f72"},{"char_end":1288,"char_start":1113,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":70525,"document_char_start":70350,"evidence_id":"ev_03c79b1bae942092","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The potentials were measured relative to the Ag/AgCl reference electrode and converted to the RHE scale in 1 M KOH (pH = 14) using the following equation: Evs RHE=Evs Ag/AgCl+","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8dc5b55f72"},{"char_end":684,"char_start":468,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4dc4c697f3eb7604","document_char_end":29201,"document_char_start":28985,"evidence_id":"ev_d7187e9e89ccffc5","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Furthermore, a two-electrode electrolyzer employing 20 wt% Pt/C supported carbon cloth as the cathode and PSCFM supported carbon cloth as the anode demonstrates stable electrolysis at 10 mA cm −2 for ~50 h (Fig. 3h).","source_sha256":"bd972cf85ddf31b6489315aa3a3069e2366061fcf0320525d8c6493126871593"},{"char_end":864,"char_start":685,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4dc4c697f3eb7604","document_char_end":29381,"document_char_start":29202,"evidence_id":"ev_607c25c5477241aa","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Notably, the voltage increases with PSCFM (1.3%) is significantly lower compared to that with PSCF (2.3%), highlighting the superior durability of PSCFM in practical applications.","source_sha256":"bd972cf85ddf31b6489315aa3a3069e2366061fcf0320525d8c6493126871593"},{"char_end":1066,"char_start":865,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4dc4c697f3eb7604","document_char_end":29583,"document_char_start":29382,"evidence_id":"ev_e6e06180466f9d49","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The Faraday efficiency of PSCFM and PSCF anode catalysts was determined by measuring the concentration of gaseous products using gas chromatography based on an efficient four-electron reaction process.","source_sha256":"bd972cf85ddf31b6489315aa3a3069e2366061fcf0320525d8c6493126871593"},{"char_end":1667,"char_start":1268,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4dc4c697f3eb7604","document_char_end":30184,"document_char_start":29785,"evidence_id":"ev_797a901e052ee681","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The durability of PSCFM was also evaluated in an alkaline water electrolyzer (membrane electrode assembly (MEA) mode) (Fig. 3i, j). Clearly, the electrolyzer equipped with a PSCFM anode and a Pt/C cathode exhibited only slight voltage vibration during continuous galvanostatic measurement at 30 mA cm −2 and 50 mA cm −2 for at least 80 h, implying its promising stability for practical applications.","source_sha256":"bd972cf85ddf31b6489315aa3a3069e2366061fcf0320525d8c6493126871593"},{"char_end":333,"char_start":120,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5e62460868a3fdf4","document_char_end":73061,"document_char_start":72848,"evidence_id":"ev_1af408efcfdbf387","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"To prepare the catalyst electrode, a catalyst ink was first prepared by sonicating a mixture of 10 mg catalyst, 10 mg acetylene black, 1 mL of absolute ethanol, and 100 μL of 5 wt% Nafion for 1.5 h in an ice bath.","source_sha256":"f6eec09560a730363bead2d31e4e5873172765bd845e7e47d5b29423d7d11920"},{"char_end":426,"char_start":334,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5e62460868a3fdf4","document_char_end":73154,"document_char_start":73062,"evidence_id":"ev_aaee99ce4ee274fd","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"This ink was then dropped onto a hemicylindrical silicon prism pre-coated with a gold layer.","source_sha256":"f6eec09560a730363bead2d31e4e5873172765bd845e7e47d5b29423d7d11920"},{"char_end":637,"char_start":427,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5e62460868a3fdf4","document_char_end":73365,"document_char_start":73155,"evidence_id":"ev_fd298b0ca47078e0","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst electrode, along with a Pt foil counter electrode and a Hg/HgO reference electrode (as shown in Supplementary Fig. 45), were used in a three-electrode configuration filled with 1 M KOH electrolyte.","source_sha256":"f6eec09560a730363bead2d31e4e5873172765bd845e7e47d5b29423d7d11920"},{"char_end":819,"char_start":638,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5e62460868a3fdf4","document_char_end":73547,"document_char_start":73366,"evidence_id":"ev_01c36a9da43c2124","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The electrode potential was systematically varied from 1.45 V to 1.85 V in steps. At each potential step, an infrared spectrum was collected with a time resolution of 10 s per scan.","source_sha256":"f6eec09560a730363bead2d31e4e5873172765bd845e7e47d5b29423d7d11920"},{"char_end":3917,"char_start":3772,"chunk_id":"mdchk_8615495d0bd58aae","document_char_end":46399,"document_char_start":46254,"evidence_id":"ev_ffd9f5fec487a555","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"In comparison, in the LOM- 34 O₂ pathway, the PDS is the absorption of OH on Ov(IS3)afterO₂ release, giving a calculated overpotential of 0.46 V.","source_sha256":"fdf887f2cdd337d04e00a8541b3784259462fded561dd4fb96bd11f4f28757ba"},{"char_end":1988,"char_start":1798,"chunk_id":"mdchk_92e080136a0b5a01","document_char_end":23806,"document_char_start":23616,"evidence_id":"ev_920c8f95da4ab186","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The PSCFM with Mn partially substituting Fe in PSCF was optimized from the second-cycle prediction, achieving a minimum predicted overpotential of 302.92 mV (322.75 mV ± 14.09 mV) (Fig. 2i).","source_sha256":"4d846ce23ac7924c7172a076a018d580e66dbaf0198b60804fe406fb5d767a6c"},{"char_end":86,"char_start":0,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":66090,"document_char_start":66004,"evidence_id":"ev_57ade4e093fc8faa","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"1.8 V vs RHE to activate the electrocatalysts and obtain a stable cyclic voltammogram.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":484,"char_start":386,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":66488,"document_char_start":66390,"evidence_id":"ev_f613d0c7c354b2fa","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"In both methods, the catalyst ink was loaded onto carbon cloth with a mass loading of 1 mg cm −2 .","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":895,"char_start":755,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":66899,"document_char_start":66759,"evidence_id":"ev_a2436405bd23bc22","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"In the three-electrode configuration, a Hg/HgO electrode and a graphite rod were used as the reference and counter electrodes, respectively.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":1267,"char_start":1138,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":67271,"document_char_start":67142,"evidence_id":"ev_3ac95a02dc13627c","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Electrochemical measurements were performed at room temperature using a CHI 760E electrochemical workstation (Chenhua, Shanghai).","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":1453,"char_start":1268,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":67457,"document_char_start":67272,"evidence_id":"ev_8313f0e7b5d9919f","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst ink was prepared by dispersing 10 mg of catalyst powder in 1 mL of anhydrous ethanol and 50 μLof anion exchange ionomer (Fumion FAA-3-SOLUT-10, FuMA-Tech) using sonication.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":1590,"char_start":1454,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":67594,"document_char_start":67458,"evidence_id":"ev_9954d3a414af14b6","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst ink was then drop-coated onto the surface of the NF electrodes to achieve desired mass loadings of 1 mg cm −2 and 3mgcm −2.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":1788,"char_start":1591,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":67792,"document_char_start":67595,"evidence_id":"ev_53a7e534067df771","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The two electrodes were separated by a pre-treated alkaline exchange membrane (Fumasep FAA-3-30, thickness ∼30 μm, FuMA- Tech), Prior to use, the membrane was immersed in 6 M KOH solution for 12 h.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":843,"char_start":739,"chunk_id":"mdchk_eb33137c2954838b","document_char_end":71370,"document_char_start":71266,"evidence_id":"ev_1d83bc3f1256cf3c","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"An Ag/AgCl electrode served as the reference electrode, and a Pt wire was used as the counter electrode.","source_sha256":"10e5ef68b2c626aca2d6642403c72781469e9dfa221a7c1a946270e1381bbed0"},{"char_end":159,"char_start":34,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":62585,"document_char_start":62460,"evidence_id":"ev_f416168ef596716b","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"A 5 mm diameter rotating disk electrode (E5 RDE, PINE) was used to evaluate the electrocatalytic properties of the catalysts.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":313,"char_start":160,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":62739,"document_char_start":62586,"evidence_id":"ev_53c10156d8c61ba3","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Cyclic vol- tammetry, LSV, EIS, chronopotentiometry and other electrochemical tests were performed using an electrochemical workstation (Corrtest 2350H).","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":422,"char_start":314,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":62848,"document_char_start":62740,"evidence_id":"ev_d5dd2960587b06dc","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"To prepare the catalyst ink, 10 mg of catalyst powder and 2 mg of acetylene black were mixed in a container.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":894,"char_start":715,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":63320,"document_char_start":63141,"evidence_id":"ev_8041a05387c56457","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The rotating disc electrode was ground with a suede soaked in alumina suspension. Subsequently, a 10 μL aliquot of the ink was pipetted onto the RDE and dried at room temperature.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":1642,"char_start":1421,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":64068,"document_char_start":63847,"evidence_id":"ev_d49b165de46e936b","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst activity for the OER was evaluated by LSV (from 1.2 to 1.8 V vs RHE at 10 mV s −1 ). Before testing, the working electrode was scanned for 10 cycles (1.2–1.8 V vs RHE) to achieve a stable cyclic voltammogram.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":1708,"char_start":1643,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":64134,"document_char_start":64069,"evidence_id":"ev_1b2371ef9b6f1831","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The Tafel curves were obtained at a slow scan rate of 1 mV s −1 .","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"}],"evidence_scope":"primary_report","instruments":[{"entity_id":"inst_f5ce371b197c0fbc","evidence_ids":["ev_3ac95a02dc13627c"],"manufacturer":"Chenhua","model":"760E","name":"CHI 760E electrochemical workstation","settings":{}},{"entity_id":"inst_d589df8868a030b1","evidence_ids":["ev_53c10156d8c61ba3"],"manufacturer":"Corrtest","model":"2350H","name":"Corrtest 2350H","settings":{}},{"entity_id":"inst_0ad749813a49fd32","evidence_ids":["ev_f416168ef596716b"],"manufacturer":"PINE","model":"E5","name":"E5 RDE","settings":{}}],"materials":[{"amount":"10 mg","entity_id":"mat_32621df7aeb389e6","evidence_ids":["ev_8313f0e7b5d9919f"],"name":"catalyst powder","pretreatment":null,"purity":null,"role":null,"supplier":null},{"amount":"50 μL","entity_id":"mat_6e4b0861874cd10d","evidence_ids":["ev_8313f0e7b5d9919f"],"name":"anion exchange ionomer","pretreatment":null,"purity":null,"role":"ionomer","supplier":"FuMA-Tech"},{"amount":null,"entity_id":"mat_0212b4ee13d3fbd9","evidence_ids":["ev_f613d0c7c354b2fa"],"name":"carbon cloth","pretreatment":null,"purity":null,"role":null,"supplier":null},{"amount":null,"entity_id":"mat_2582bb7d894ba7d8","evidence_ids":["ev_a2436405bd23bc22"],"name":"Hg/HgO electrode","pretreatment":null,"purity":null,"role":null,"supplier":null},{"amount":null,"entity_id":"mat_1ecadbd4ded15056","evidence_ids":["ev_a2436405bd23bc22"],"name":"graphite rod","pretreatment":null,"purity":null,"role":"counter electrode","supplier":null},{"amount":null,"entity_id":"mat_d8c05