on_id":"rel_7198d824b6c53394","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_e6e06180466f9d49"],"object_id":"step_f500d57f7c22d00f","predicate":"has_step","relation_id":"rel_5c05d6b637fcd227","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_797a901e052ee681"],"object_id":"step_fc7ee1b9f86f6384","predicate":"has_step","relation_id":"rel_b0e31e0126c7d2d0","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_e6e06180466f9d49"],"object_id":"char_c586a5b655618005","predicate":"uses_characterization","relation_id":"rel_04324bdc374703e2","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_607c25c5477241aa"],"object_id":"result_4df90b79b8ca9a1e","predicate":"reports_result","relation_id":"rel_350bf8123ea3a26b","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_920c8f95da4ab186"],"object_id":"result_1bbd14b29b0b483e","predicate":"reports_result","relation_id":"rel_163b3250d53847fa","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_ffd9f5fec487a555"],"object_id":"result_a8e159ca06fb77ad","predicate":"reports_result","relation_id":"rel_ebffd5e8c09a6b35","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"},{"evidence_ids":["ev_03c79b1bae942092"],"object_id":"caveat_90b171099906a6d8","predicate":"has_caveat","relation_id":"rel_e9f1eb620517761f","subject_id":"protocol_5200909154b395d9"}],"results":[{"context":"Notably, the voltage increases with PSCFM (1.3%) is significantly lower compared to that with PSCF (2.3%), highlighting the superior durability of PSCFM in practical applications.","evidence_ids":["ev_607c25c5477241aa"],"metric":"voltage increase","raw_value":"1.3%","result_id":"result_4df90b79b8ca9a1e"},{"context":"The PSCFM with Mn partially substituting Fe in PSCF was optimized from the second-cycle prediction, achieving a minimum predicted overpotential of 302.92 mV (322.75 mV ± 14.09 mV) (Fig. 2i).","evidence_ids":["ev_920c8f95da4ab186"],"metric":"predicted overpotential","raw_value":"302.92 mV","result_id":"result_1bbd14b29b0b483e"},{"context":"In comparison, in the LOM- 34 O₂ pathway, the PDS is the absorption of OH on Ov(IS3)afterO₂ release, giving a calculated overpotential of 0.46 V.","evidence_ids":["ev_ffd9f5fec487a555"],"metric":"calculated overpotential","raw_value":"0.46 V","result_id":"result_a8e159ca06fb77ad"}],"schema_version":"domain-adapter-knowledge-v0.1","software":[],"source_chunk_ids":["mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","mdchk_4dc4c697f3eb7604","mdchk_5e62460868a3fdf4","mdchk_8615495d0bd58aae","mdchk_92e080136a0b5a01","mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","mdchk_eb33137c2954838b","mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88"],"source_paper_tier":"primary_oer","steps":[{"action":"The catalyst ink was prepared by dispersing 10 mg of catalyst powder in 1 mL of anhydrous ethanol and 50 μLof anion exchange ionomer (Fumion FAA-3-SOLUT-10, FuMA-Tech) using sonication.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_8313f0e7b5d9919f"],"notes":null,"order":1,"step_id":"step_5e0d3cdeda7078e4"},{"action":"The catalyst ink was then drop-coated onto the surface of the NF electrodes to achieve desired mass loadings of 1 mg cm −2 and 3mgcm −2.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_9954d3a414af14b6"],"notes":null,"order":2,"step_id":"step_e98c32b262691cbd"},{"action":"1.8 V vs RHE to activate the electrocatalysts and obtain a stable cyclic voltammogram.","conditions":["1.8 V vs RHE"],"evidence_ids":["ev_57ade4e093fc8faa"],"notes":null,"order":3,"step_id":"step_d49ffbd3cc2b33e5"},{"action":"The rotating disc electrode was ground with a suede soaked in alumina suspension. Subsequently, a 10 μL aliquot of the ink was pipetted onto the RDE and dried at room temperature.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_8041a05387c56457"],"notes":null,"order":4,"step_id":"step_b6c4d99f3db72161"},{"action":"The catalyst activity for the OER was evaluated by LSV (from 1.2 to 1.8 V vs RHE at 10 mV s −1 ). Before testing, the working electrode was scanned for 10 cycles (1.2–1.8 V vs RHE) to achieve a stable cyclic voltammogram.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_d49b165de46e936b"],"notes":null,"order":5,"step_id":"step_2417c4550b78f275"},{"action":"The Tafel curves were obtained at a slow scan rate of 1 mV s −1 .","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_1b2371ef9b6f1831"],"notes":null,"order":6,"step_id":"step_46b15742f72e8a3f"},{"action":"The catalyst ink was prepared by sonicating a mixture of 3 mg catalyst, 500 μL deionized water, 460 μLabsoluteethanol,and40μLof5wt%Nafion for 1.5 h in an ice bath.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_fe33583ca0f97f77"],"notes":null,"order":7,"step_id":"step_c8ee2d23fc457a95"},{"action":"To prepare the catalyst electrode, a catalyst ink was first prepared by sonicating a mixture of 10 mg catalyst, 10 mg acetylene black, 1 mL of absolute ethanol, and 100 μL of 5 wt% Nafion for 1.5 h in an ice bath.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_1af408efcfdbf387"],"notes":null,"order":8,"step_id":"step_4ea3573c4f760996"},{"action":"This ink was then dropped onto a hemicylindrical silicon prism pre-coated with a gold layer.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_aaee99ce4ee274fd"],"notes":null,"order":9,"step_id":"step_789390e8484152ea"},{"action":"The electrode potential was systematically varied from 1.45 V to 1.85 V in steps. At each potential step, an infrared spectrum was collected with a time resolution of 10 s per scan.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_01c36a9da43c2124"],"notes":null,"order":10,"step_id":"step_5de9d25386a5267a"},{"action":"Furthermore, a two-electrode electrolyzer employing 20 wt% Pt/C supported carbon cloth as the cathode and PSCFM supported carbon cloth as the anode demonstrates stable electrolysis at 10 mA cm −2 for ~50 h (Fig. 3h).","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_d7187e9e89ccffc5"],"notes":null,"order":11,"step_id":"step_e272ca3d4b10d663"},{"action":"The Faraday efficiency of PSCFM and PSCF anode catalysts was determined by measuring the concentration of gaseous products using gas chromatography based on an efficient four-electron reaction process.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_e6e06180466f9d49"],"notes":null,"order":12,"step_id":"step_f500d57f7c22d00f"},{"action":"The durability of PSCFM was also evaluated in an alkaline water electrolyzer (membrane electrode assembly (MEA) mode) (Fig. 3i, j). Clearly, the electrolyzer equipped with a PSCFM anode and a Pt/C cathode exhibited only slight voltage vibration during continuous galvanostatic measurement at 30 mA cm −2 and 50 mA cm −2 for at least 80 h, implying its promising stability for practical applications.","conditions":[],"evidence_ids":["ev_797a901e052ee681"],"notes":null,"order":13,"step_id":"step_fc7ee1b9f86f6384"}]}
